cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "emu_pk: a differentiable linear matter power spectrum emulator"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the works it builds on."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Comparat
    given-names: Johan
    email: jcomparat@lpsc.in2p3.fr
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9200-1497"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JohanComparat/emu_pk"
url: "https://emu-pk.readthedocs.io/en/stable/"
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 2.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-06"
abstract: >-
  emu_pk emulates the linear matter power spectrum over an eleven-parameter
  cosmology, with three separate neutrino masses, CPL dark energy and spatial
  curvature, to k = 300 h/Mpc and z = 5. It is written in JAX and is
  differentiable, so derivatives with respect to cosmological parameters come
  from automatic differentiation rather than finite differences. Two of those
  derivatives are exact by construction, because the primordial power law is
  divided out of the training target and restored analytically. The training
  truth is CAMB at raised precision, multiplied by the reionization heating of
  a CLASS pair at the same point, and the network is scored against a
  converged CAMB reference it was not trained on.
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      CosmoPower: emulating cosmological power spectra for accelerated Bayesian
      inference from next-generation surveys
    authors:
      - family-names: "Spurio Mancini"
        given-names: A.
      - family-names: Piras
        given-names: D.
      - family-names: Alsing
        given-names: J.
      - family-names: Joachimi
        given-names: B.
