        given-names: M. P.
    journal: "Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society"
    volume: 511
    issue: 2
    start: 1771
    end: 1788
    year: 2022
    doi: 10.1093/mnras/stac064
    notes: >-
      The network architecture and the learned activation are theirs; emu_pk
      reproduces both and differs in the training box, the wavenumber reach and
      the training target.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      The Cosmic Linear Anisotropy Solving System (CLASS). Part II:
      Approximation schemes
    authors:
      - family-names: Blas
        given-names: Diego
      - family-names: Lesgourgues
        given-names: Julien
      - family-names: Tram
        given-names: Thomas
    journal: "Journal of Cosmology and Astroparticle Physics"
    volume: 2011
    issue: 07
    start: 034
    year: 2011
    doi: 10.1088/1475-7516/2011/07/034
    notes: >-
      Every training spectrum carries CLASS's reionization heating, as the
      ratio of a CLASS pair with and without it, and the correction table in
      emu_pk.ratio is distilled from CLASS directly.
  - type: article
    title: "Efficient computation of CMB anisotropies in closed FRW models"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lewis
        given-names: Antony
      - family-names: Challinor
        given-names: Anthony
      - family-names: Lasenby
        given-names: Anthony
    journal: "The Astrophysical Journal"
    volume: 538
    start: 473
    end: 476
    year: 2000
    doi: 10.1086/309179
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/astro-ph/9911177"
    notes: >-
      CAMB. Every training spectrum and every validation truth is a CAMB
      solve, at raised precision for training and at a converged setting for
      the reference.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      CSST cosmological emulator I: Matter power spectrum emulation with one
      percent accuracy to k = 10 h/Mpc
    authors:
      - family-names: Chen
        given-names: Zhao
      - family-names: Yu
